    {
      "id": "t028",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 1995.5000000000002,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 25.2,
      "text": "Where are we?",
      "weight": 700,
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t029",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2036.4000000000003,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 49.7,
      "text": "“Weavers, weaving at break of day,<br>Why do you weave a garment so gay?”",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t030",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2092.3,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 19.3,
      "text": "Sarojini Naidu, <em>Indian Weavers</em>. The presentation opened with it.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t031",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2147.6000000000004,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 77.9,
      "text": "There is a major dilemma between the craft and the machines on how to coexist in this world where technology is advancing with every passing day. With the powerlooms taking over, what then happens to the craft of weaving and how relevant is it to today’s society?",
      "size": "s",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "p032",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2255.1000000000004,
      "w": 341,
      "h": 213,
      "src": "projects/media/narayanpet-weavers-centre/loom-1.jpg",
      "fit": "cover",
      "alt": "A weaver in a white cap working at a handloom",
      "anim": {
        "enter": {
          "on": true,
          "from": {
            "opacity": 0,
            "y": 40
          },
          "dur": 0.9,
          "delay": 0,
          "ease": "out"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p033",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 627,
      "y": 2255.1000000000004,
      "w": 341,
      "h": 213,
      "src": "projects/media/narayanpet-weavers-centre/loom-2.jpg",
      "fit": "cover",
      "alt": "A woman weaving at a wooden handloom",
      "anim": {
        "enter": {
          "on": true,
          "from": {
            "opacity": 0,
            "y": 40
          },
          "dur": 0.9,
          "delay": 0,
          "ease": "out"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t034",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2504.1000000000004,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 97.2,
      "text": "Through brainstorming, interviews, and researched, we concluded that  the only way to move ahead would be to elevate the craft of Handloom and create awareness about its essence and beauty. It’s more than just a commodity. Along with the physical effort, it also takes creativity and human connection to create every product.",
      "size": "s",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t035",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 2641.6000000000004,
      "w": 222,
      "h": 25.2,
      "text": "the question",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t036",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2641.6000000000004,
      "w": 698,
      "h": 124.6,
      "text": "How might we elevate the craft of Handloom and create awareness about its essence and beauty? ",
      "size": "l",
      "weight": 700,
      "color": "accent",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t037",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 32,
      "y": 2927.1000000000004,
      "w": 222,
      "h": 25.2,
      "text": "research",
      "color": "mute",
      "nav": "research",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t038",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2927.1000000000004,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 25.2,
      "text": "What we heard?",
      "weight": 700,
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t039",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 2968.0000000000005,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 19.3,
      "text": "Weavers and townspeople of Narayanpet.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "p040",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 3011.3000000000006,
      "w": 341,
      "h": 378,
      "src": "projects/media/narayanpet-weavers-centre/weaver.jpg",
      "fit": "cover",
      "alt": "An elderly man in white seated on a bench in a Narayanpet house",
      "anim": {
        "enter": {
          "on": true,
          "from": {
            "opacity": 0,
            "y": 40
          },
          "dur": 0.9,
          "delay": 0,
          "ease": "out"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t041",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 627,
      "y": 3131.3000000000006,
      "w": 341,
      "h": 74.9,
      "text": "“We’re all lost. Our houses and livelihood is designed around the functioning of a loom. We work and live here.”",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t042",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 627,
      "y": 3212.100000000001,
      "w": 341,
      "h": 38.5,
      "text": "Homes in Narayanpet are built around the loom, which is where the architecture starts.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t043",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 3449.3000000000006,
      "w": 301,
      "h": 124.6,
      "text": "“Since 1980, our importance started declining and the younger generation doesn’t want to continue the traditions anymore. They can earn more by working for just 2 hours in the city.”",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t044",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 618,
      "y": 3497.3000000000006,
      "w": 350,
      "h": 74.9,
      "text": "“People are migrating to bigger cities for better job opportunities and pay as they don’t see a future in weaving.”",
      "align": "right",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t045",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 3588.0000000000005,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 19.3,
      "text": "Two people, the same story: the young are leaving the loom for the city.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t046",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 349,
      "y": 3677.3000000000006,
      "w": 619,
      "h": 124.7,
      "text": "“The situation is very dire and we feel like we’re on the verge of dying, almost like on ventilators.”",
      "size": "l",
      "align": "right",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t047",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 349,
      "y": 3812.600000000001,
      "w": 619,
      "h": 19.3,
      "text": "How the weavers described where the craft stands today.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "align": "right",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t048",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 3891.900000000001,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 74.9,
      "text": "“If people start getting paid better, the situation will slowly will start getting better and the weavers will come back to weaving.”",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t049",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 3972.700000000001,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 19.3,
      "text": "What would bring them back.",
      "size": "s",
      "color": "mute",
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t050",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 4102.000000000001,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 25.2,
      "text": "Understanding the urban texture of Narayanpet",
      "weight": 700,
      "anim": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "t051",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 4142.900000000001,
      "w": 460,
      "h": 57.9,
      "text": "Narrow streets, colonnade spaces, courtyard houses, jharokhas, raised plinths, colourful fenestrations and walls, weaving looms in every household, and goldsmith shops.",
      "size": "s",
      "anim": {}
    },
